---
import LaunchLayout from "../layouts/LaunchLayout.astro";
import { REPOSITORY, REVIEWED_SOURCE } from "../config/launch";
const source = `${REPOSITORY}/blob/${REVIEWED_SOURCE}`;
---
<LaunchLayout title="Evidence & claim boundaries | Velvet" description="Inspect Velvet's public evidence. Separate synthetic fixtures, local implementation results, and roadmap hypotheses before making a broader claim.">
  <div class="l-wrap l-page"><div class="l-page-head"><p class="l-eyebrow">Evidence room</p><h1>Inspectable results.<br />Explicit boundaries.</h1><p class="l-lede">Every result needs an environment, an observation method, and a limit. These are public reference demonstrations, not customer deployments.</p></div>
    <div class="l-grid">
      <article class="l-card"><span class="l-tag">Synthetic local fixture</span><h3>One blocked route. Eight observed effects.</h3><p>The named account-disable route is denied while eight declared alternative routes reach the prohibited state. The recorded verdict is <code>CONTROL_FALSE_SUCCESS</code>.</p><p><strong>Establishes:</strong> the measurement method and an inspectable example of a route/effect mismatch.</p><p><strong>Does not establish:</strong> a vendor vulnerability, a discovery rate, or coverage of undeclared paths.</p><a href="/replay/">Replay the recorded result ↗</a><p class="l-fine"><a href={`${source}/benchmarks/agent_authorization/shadowpath/SHADOWPATH_RESULTS.md`}>Pinned result and provenance</a></p></article>
      <article class="l-card"><span class="l-tag">Local PostgreSQL reference</span><h3>Authorization at the commit boundary.</h3><p>The protected-refund reference reconciles four committed refunds totaling $100 under a $100 budget, with workflow closure and a signed observer checkpoint.</p><p><strong>Establishes:</strong> a bounded single-database contract and independently runnable evidence verification.</p><p><strong>Does not establish:</strong> actual payment-provider settlement, an independent security audit, or measured production throughput.</p><a href="/protected-refunds/">Inspect the reference ledger ↗</a><p class="l-fine"><a href={`${source}/docs/public/protected-refunds.md`}>Pinned contract and assumptions</a></p></article>
      <article class="l-card"><span class="l-tag">Implemented components</span><h3>Assessment, execution, evidence.</h3><p>The repository contains ShadowPath effect projects, a Rust MCP proxy, exact-bound execution permits, evidence tooling, and outcome portfolios.</p><p><strong>Establishes:</strong> inspectable implementation surfaces and explicit supported paths.</p><p><strong>Does not establish:</strong> a hosted service, complete protocol coverage, or prevention of actions outside the integrated boundary.</p><a href={`${source}/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`}>Inspect implementation status ↗</a></article>
    </div>
    <section class="l-page-section l-prose"><h2>Check the claim, not only the signature.</h2><p>Pin the source revision, configuration, contract, and trusted public keys. Keep dispatch evidence separate from the state observer. Record inconclusive results and missing routes rather than treating them as successful prevention.</p><p>A signed artifact authenticates a record under its stated trust assumptions. It does not show that the record is the latest one, that every relevant route was covered, or that the business effect could not happen elsewhere.</p><div class="l-callout"><p>The browser replay shows a committed synthetic result. Clicking it does not run a fresh assessment, contact a vendor, or operate a customer system.</p></div><p>Public case studies are published only when the underlying evidence is cleared for disclosure. Private correspondence and reproduction packages are not part of this site.</p><p class="l-fine">Evidence links above pin the reviewed implementation to <code>{REVIEWED_SOURCE}</code>. Review current implementation status separately when evaluating a later revision.</p></section>
    <div class="l-actions"><a class="l-button" href="/pilot/">Build a baseline for your workflow ↗</a><a class="l-button l-button-quiet" href={`${REPOSITORY}/blob/main/docs/public/claims-evidence.md`}>Read the claims register</a></div>
  </div>
</LaunchLayout>
